{
  "id": "ruff",
  "name": "Ruff",
  "about": "Lint and formatting for Python",
  "needs": [
    "ruff"
  ],
  "install": [
    {
      "about": "ruff, with uv",
      "run": [
        "uv",
        "tool",
        "install",
        "ruff"
      ],
      "unless": "ruff"
    },
    {
      "about": "ruff, with pipx",
      "run": [
        "pipx",
        "install",
        "ruff"
      ],
      "unless": "ruff"
    },
    {
      "about": "a virtual environment for ruff",
      "run": [
        "python3",
        "-m",
        "venv",
        "${tools}/venv/ruff"
      ],
      "unless": "ruff"
    },
    {
      "about": "ruff, into that environment",
      "run": [
        "${tools}/venv/ruff/bin/pip",
        "install",
        "--quiet",
        "ruff"
      ],
      "when": "${tools}/venv/ruff/bin/pip",
      "unless": "ruff"
    },
    {
      "about": "putting ruff on the path",
      "run": [
        "ln",
        "-sf",
        "${tools}/venv/ruff/bin/ruff",
        "${bin}/ruff"
      ],
      "when": "${tools}/venv/ruff/bin/ruff",
      "unless": "ruff"
    }
  ],
  "uninstall": [
    {
      "run": [
        "uv",
        "tool",
        "uninstall",
        "ruff"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "see": "https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/installation/",
  "languages": {
    "python": {
      "servers": [
        {
          "name": "ruff",
          "command": "ruff",
          "args": [
            "server"
          ],
          "roots": [
            "pyproject.toml",
            "ruff.toml",
            ".ruff.toml",
            ".git"
          ],
          "env": {
            "VIRTUAL_ENV": "${venv}",
            "PATH": "${venv_bin}:${env:PATH}"
          },
          "settings": {
            "settings": {
              "interpreter": [
                "${python}"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "_about": [
    "uv and pipx each put a tool in a virtual environment of its own, which is",
    "what you want: ruff's dependencies never meet your project's.",
    "",
    "The last resort makes that environment by hand, because plain `pip",
    "install --user` is not an option any more \u2014 every current distribution",
    "marks its Python as externally managed (PEP 668) and refuses, and on the",
    "machines where it would still work it drops packages into a shared",
    "user-site directory rather than an environment of their own."
  ]
}
